{
  "id": "trust-001",
  "description": "(0.5.0, Draft) Registry trust-list known answer (RFC-ACDP-0020 §4–§6), executed by scripts/conformance-runner.py. Vector 1 is a golden acdp:trust-list body issued by the sig-003 did:key test issuer: JCS canonical form, content_hash and the Ed25519 signature over the ASCII content_hash, exactly as sig-003, plus the §4.1 body constraints and the §5.2 step 4 runtime rules. Vector 2 is an evaluation table: each case gives a body's identity fields, an optional verified receipt (its registry_did and the fingerprint of the key that signed it), optional advertised profiles and T, and the RFC-ACDP-0020 §6.2 outcome, reason and deciding entry. Timestamps are canonical, so the runner compares them as strings. Test keypair MUST NOT be used in production.",
  "tags": [
    "trust-list",
    "consumer",
    "offline",
    "0.5.0",
    "known-answer",
    "golden"
  ],
  "applies_to_profiles": [
    "acdp-consumer-trust-list"
  ],
  "test_keypair": {
